# Public API

## Facade (browser parity)

```php
Talaria::init([...]);
Talaria::logger(['tags' => [...], 'minLevel' => 'error']);
Talaria::withTags([...]);
Talaria::debug/info/warning/warn/error/fatal($message, $context);
Talaria::log($level, $message, $context);
Talaria::captureException($e, $context);
Talaria::captureMessage($message, $level, $context);
Talaria::getMinLevel(); Talaria::setMinLevel($level); Talaria::isLevelEnabled($level);
Talaria::flush();
Talaria::close();
```

Also expose `Talaria\TalariaClient` for DI and `Talaria\Logger` (PSR-3 + scoped helpers).
`Talaria\Client` remains a deprecated class alias of `TalariaClient`.

`Talaria\Logger::log()` must keep **untyped** `$level` / `$message` parameters so the class
implements psr/log 1.x, 2.x, and 3.x. Do not add `\Stringable|string` on `$message` —
that fatals against older `LoggerInterface::log($level, $message, …)`. Document PSR-3 in
PHPDoc; cast with `(string) $message` at runtime.

## Init options

- Required: `dsn` or `baseUrl`, `apiKey`, `environment`
- Optional: `release`, `sampleRate`, `minLevel` (default `debug`), `beforeSend`, `maxBatchSize`, `flushIntervalMs`, `defaultIntegrations`, `userId`, `tags`, `httpTimeoutSeconds`
- `TalariaClient::addProcessor()` for per-request tag/extra enrichment (prefer over `setTags` on long-lived singletons)
- Tag merge order (later wins): automatic `RuntimeContext` tags → init/global → processors → logger scope → per-call context

## Capture rules

- Exceptions default `level: error`; messages default `info`
- Derive `eventType` from level
- Context bag: `tags`, `extra`, `userId`, `title`, optional `mechanism` (`type` / `handled` / `synthetic`)
- `captureException` builds first-class `exception.values[]` (frames oldest→newest, `functionName`); `extra` is app metadata only
- Gates: `minLevel` → `sampleRate` → `beforeSend`; filtered captures are quiet no-ops
- Scoped loggers can only raise the effective minLevel floor
- Capture enqueues only — network I/O happens on queue drain
